---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import HeroStudies from '../../components/hero-studies/HeroStudies';
---
<SiteLayout title="Hero studies · OPFS VFS" description="Internal animation studies for the OPFS VFS homepage." noindex>
  <HeroStudies client:only="react" />
  <details class="study-brief">
    <summary>The design prompt</summary>
    <p><strong>Latest direction: Layers.</strong> Replace physical disk hardware with three thin, rounded rectangular layers, slightly separated and viewed from above at an angle. Files converge into the gaps. Soft pulses travel across the layers. Use neutral translucent materials, muted file colors, and a transparent canvas.</p>
    <p>Build a Three.js hero animation for OPFS VFS from this description, without a reference image. Place a full-width scene below the headline on a transparent canvas. Leave generous negative space. No backdrop, enclosing panel, floor, or vignette.</p>
    <p>Create a finely detailed, shallow cylindrical storage device on the right. Show it from an elevated three-quarter angle, with an elliptical top face and enough side visible to convey thickness. Use subtle concentric machining, layered edges, and a recessed center. Avoid a vertical, front-facing coin.</p>
    <p>Thousands of small file objects travel from the left into the disk along a few graceful curved paths. Nearby files are larger and more detailed; distant files become fine points. Some carry readable SQL, MD, TS, XLS, PDF, and JPG labels with understated document details.</p>
    <p>Use satin silver and neutral graphite, with small emerald accents at the intake. File types may use muted blue, amber, lilac, and green. Avoid an overall green tint, neon, or heavy bloom. Adapt materials and lighting to both the warm light theme and charcoal dark theme.</p>
    <p>Loop continuously. Files gently accelerate toward the intake and disappear inside it. Keep the camera stable, with subtle disk movement. Place OPFS VFS below the disk as HTML text. Preserve mobile composition, reduced-motion support, and efficient rendering.</p>
  </details>
</SiteLayout>
